1. Description

    Implemented the Automated Medicine Refill Workflow for the Pharma Store to automate recurring medicine orders based on active customer subscriptions.

    The workflow connects the subscription schedule with the refill/order process so that medicines can be prepared for the customer's next scheduled delivery without requiring the customer to manually place the same order each time.

    The implementation also provides delivery-date tracking, refill status management, and a foundation for customer notifications and recurring order processing.

2. Business Requirement

    Customers who subscribe to regularly required medicines should not need to manually reorder them for every delivery cycle.

    The automated refill workflow is designed to:

    Monitor active medicine subscriptions.
    Identify upcoming refill dates.
    Generate or prepare recurring medicine orders.
    Maintain the subscribed quantity.
    Calculate the next delivery date.
    Update refill status.
    Handle skipped or paused subscriptions.
    Support customer notifications.
    Reduce manual reordering.


3. Automated Refill Workflow

    The complete workflow follows:

    Active Subscription
           ↓
    Check Next Refill Date
           ↓
    Refill Date Reached
           ↓
    Validate Subscription
           ↓
    Check Product Availability
           ↓
    Create Recurring Order
           ↓
    Update Refill Status
           ↓
    Schedule Next Delivery
           ↓
    Notify Customer
           ↓
    Order Processing
           ↓
    Delivery

    This creates a continuous recurring medicine cycle.

4. Subscription Eligibility Check
 
    Before creating a refill, the workflow verifies that the subscription is eligible.

    The system checks:

     Subscription status.
     Customer information.
     Product information.
     Subscription quantity.
     Delivery frequency.
     Next refill date.
     Product availability.

     Only valid active subscriptions should proceed to the refill process.

5. Refill Date Management

    Each subscription maintains a scheduled refill/delivery date.

    Example:

     Subscription
         ↓
     Next Refill Date
     15 September 2026
         ↓
     Refill Processing
         ↓
     Next Refill Date
     15 October 2026

     The next refill date is recalculated based on the configured subscription frequency.

6. Automated Order Creation

    When the refill date is reached, the workflow prepares a recurring order using the subscription information.

    The order contains:

     Customer
     Product
     Quantity
     Price
     Delivery Information
     Subscription Reference
     Refill Reference

    Example:

     Customer:
     Customer Name


    Medicine:
    Metformin 500 mg


    Quantity:
    2 Packs


    Subscription:
    Every 30 Days


    Refill:
    September Cycle


    Status:
    Processing


7. Product Availability Validation

    Before processing the refill, product availability is checked.

    Product Available
    Subscription
        ↓
    Product Available
        ↓
    Create Refill Order
        ↓
    Continue Processing
    Product Unavailable
    Subscription
        ↓
    Product Unavailable
        ↓
    Refill Cannot Be Processed
        ↓
    Update Refill Status
        ↓
    Notify Customer / Admin

    This helps prevent failed recurring orders caused by unavailable products.

8. Refill Status Management

     Implemented status tracking for the refill process.

     Example statuses:

      Scheduled
      Processing
      Order Created
      Pending
      Completed
      Skipped
      Failed

      This allows both users and administrators to understand the current state of a refill.

9. Pause Subscription Handling

    If a customer pauses their subscription:

    Active
      ↓
    Pause
      ↓
    Paused
      ↓
    Refill Temporarily Stopped

    The automated refill process should not create a recurring order while the subscription remains paused.

    When the customer resumes the subscription:

    Paused
      ↓
    Resume
      ↓
    Active
      ↓
    Refill Scheduling Resumes


10. Skip Next Delivery

     The workflow supports skipping the next scheduled refill without cancelling the entire subscription.

     Example:

      Next Refill
      15 September


      Customer selects:
      Skip Next Delivery


            ↓


      September Refill Skipped


            ↓


       Next Refill
       15 October

       The subscription remains active after the skipped cycle.

11. Subscription Cancellation

     When a subscription is cancelled:

     Active
       ↓
     Cancel
       ↓
     Cancelled
       ↓
     Automatic Refill Disabled

     No future recurring refill should be generated after cancellation.

12. Automated Refill Scheduler

     The workflow can be executed through a scheduled background process.

     Conceptually:

     Scheduled Job
         ↓
     Find Active Subscriptions
         ↓
     Check Refill Dates
         ↓
     Identify Due Refills
         ↓
     Validate Products
         ↓
     Create Orders
         ↓
     Update Subscription
         ↓
     Schedule Next Refill

     This removes the requirement for manual staff intervention for every recurring order.

